{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041122-echoes-sleepwalker-merits","id":1041122,"title":"Echoes (Sleepwalker Merits)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-30T23:17:55-08:00","id":1041122,"title":"Echoes (Sleepwalker Merits)","content":"This is something I've had for a little bit that I figured I'd share. It's a nifty little idea that took heavy inspiration from wolfblooded's tells, and I figured that I'd post it for thoughts, feedbacks and - just as important - ideas as to what might make good versions behind these little echoes. <hr /><br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers are an invaluable resource for the Awakened. While a Sleepwalker cannot use any of the powers a mage does or touch the Supernal, she can support the mage by standing with her. Some Sleepwalkers take it upon themselves to accept the magicks that mages place upon them, to stand next to the Awakened as caretakers of their works, footsoldiers in their battles, and custodians of their treasures. These Sleepwalkers come in contact time and time again to the supernal, and sometimes the effects that are placed on them don't always leave when the spell wears off and the magic withers. The Nimbus of the mage who places their magic on the sleepwalker lingers and seeps in, creating a unique effect which forever stains the Sleepwalkers Soul: An Echo of that Mages power.<br /> <br /> Mechanically Soul Echoes are basically merits which only Sleepwalkers can take. They represent magic that has been seeped into the Sleepwalkers soul to the point where they always bear the mark of that magic. Soul Echoes are supernatural in nature, yet they do not typically alert the awakened peripheral senses - they are passive abilities that are always there. Many Sleepwalkers can only bear a single echo upon their soul - stain the soul too much, and you begin to lose sight of it's original picture. Soul Echoes can occur from any influence involving both the Supernal and the Abyss, though Abyssal Soul Echoes usually form on the soul of a Sleeper rather than a Sleepwalker - unless the mage who has been using that Sleeper is a Scelestus or incredibly unwise in their use of reach.<br /> <br /> Soul Echoes are a phenomena only available to Sleepwalkers without any true connection to the Supernal. Proximi and Awakened have a closer connection to the Supernal, and their ability to wield these powers seems to also prevent them from gaining these echoes. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soul Echo: Quick Learner (\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Your character has been repeatedly subjected to spells that grant him a wealth of knowledge, even when he did not have that knowledge prior. You remember knowing the bits and pieces of each skill and applying them, but the vast wealth of knowledge is lost. The Supernal has left small memory dots, and your character has the capacity to draw a line to connect them. Every time you raise a skill with experience, your character regains one beat. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soul Echo: Transcendent (\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Your character has time and again been pushed beyond the limitations of human capacity. The alien mindset and physiology that is required for such inhuman capabilities has left it's mark, and while your character might not still have that capability, their mind and body has become shifted enough that the capacity for it is offered. At three dots, this merit grants a dot in a single skill. At five dots, this merit grants a dot in a single attribute. This dot may go beyond 5. This merit may only be taken once. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soul Echo: Magic Resistance (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Your character has been subject to spell after spell, and instead of being stained beneficially, his soul seems to now reject all magic. Whenever a spell is cast that targets her, the Sleepwalker treats her dots in this merit as an additional Withstand Rating.<br /> Drawback: This ability works even on effects that would benefit the Sleepwalker, including healing effects. While the Sleepwalker can lower this resistance as any withstand, she must consciously do so. If she is unconscious or preoccupied with a stressful situation such as combat, she cannot lower her guard and these things are withstood per usual. In addition, the Magic Resistance is a deep-stain on the Sleepwalkers Soul - they cannot take other Soul Echoes with this. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soul Echo: No Reflection (\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Your character has been subject to spells of espionage. Pieces of him were erased from the world to better make him invisible. The thing is - some parts of him didn't come back. His shadow, his voice, his echo. He no longer registers to any electronic devices or reflective devices. He never casts a shadow. Even mundane eyes seem to glance right off him, causing a -2 penalty to any perception attempts to notice him.<br /> Drawback: In addition to having a noticable tell of the supernatural, this makes communication difficult with people - your voice and face do not travel through mediums, which means your relegated to text. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Soul Echo: Dead Flesh (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Through constant exposure to necromantic magic, your character carries the weight of death in his skin. Perhaps that resurrection spell didn't quite fully take. Perhaps a spell designed to simulate death worked a little too well, and the side effects. Your character no longer suffers lethal damage from nonmagic sources - it is all downgraded to bashing automatically, no matter how it hits him.<br /> Drawback: For all mundane purposes, your character is dead. Heat Signatures note him at room temperature, and medical examinations show no heart beat. Devices designed to measure such things, like lie detectors, automatically fail to work on him. Life sight and magical senses don't detect this, however - simply Fallen devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}